,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":80.53110481,"data":"To expand the expression \\((2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1)\\), we distribute each term of the first polynomial to each term of the second polynomial. First, distribute \\(2z^2\\) across the second polynomial: \\[2z^2 \\cdot 3z^3 = 6z^5\\] \\[2z^2 \\cdot (-2z) = -4z^3\\] \\[2z^2 \\cdot 1 = 2z^2\\] Next, distribute \\(5z\\) across the second polynomial: \\[5z \\cdot 3z^3 = 15z^4\\] \\[5z \\cdot (-2z) = -10z^2\\] \\[5z \\cdot 1 = 5z\\] Finally, distribute \\(-6\\) across the second polynomial: \\[-6 \\cdot 3z^3 = -18z^3\\] \\[-6 \\cdot (-2z) = 12z\\] \\[-6 \\cdot 1 = -6\\] Now, combine all these terms together: \\[6z^5 - 4z^3 + 2z^2 + 15z^4 - 10z^2 + 5z - 18z^3 + 12z - 6\\] Combine like terms: \\[6z^5 + 15z^4 + (-4z^3 - 18z^3) + (2z^2 - 10z^2) + (5z + 12z) - 6\\] Simplify further: \\[6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6\\] Thus, the expanded form of \\((2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1)\\) is \\[6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6\\] \\[ \\boxed{6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6} \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":80.531117171,"data":"[Final answer] 6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6\u003c|endoftext|\u003e\n"}
